  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohammd Anis vs The State Of Bihar on 24 January, 2013 Author: Dinesh Kumar Singh Bench: Dinesh Kumar Singh In The High Court Of Judicature At Patna Criminal Miscellaneous No.48438 of 2012 ====================================================== Mohammd Anis .... .... Petitioner Versus The State Of Bihar .... .... Opposite Party/ ====================================================== Coram: Honourable Mr. Justice Dinesh Kumar Singh Oral Order",
    "facts": "The petitioner is apprehending arrest in a case registered for the offences punishable under Sections 406 and 420 of the Indian Penal Code and Sections 51 and 59 of the Food and Safety Standard Act. It is alleged that the wheat in the go-down of the petitioner who was the Assistant Go-down Manager of the Food Corporation, unit Khagaria were found to be sub-standard.",
    "arguments": "It is submitted by learned counsel for the petitioner that the grains were supplied by the FSS and for standard quality, the petitioner cannot be held responsible when the search seizure were not made as per the FCC regulations.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is submitted by learned counsel for the petitioner that the grains were supplied by the FSS and for standard quality, the petitioner cannot be held responsible when the search seizure were not made as per the FCC regulations.",
